---
import Explainer from '../../components/Explainer.astro';
import Tool from '../../layouts/Tool.astro';
---

<Tool
  path="/tools/aadhaar-masker/"
  title="Mask Aadhaar Online: Hide the First 8 Digits"
  description="Hide the first 8 digits of your Aadhaar number, or anything else on an ID, before you share a copy. Works on photos, scans and e-Aadhaar PDFs. Free."
  heading="Mask your Aadhaar number"
  faq={[
    [
      'What is a masked Aadhaar?',
      'A copy of your Aadhaar where the first 8 digits of the number are replaced, for example with X, and only the last 4 digits can be read. UIDAI offers it as an option when you download your e-Aadhaar.',
    ],
    [
      'Is a masked Aadhaar valid for KYC?',
      'UIDAI issues masked e-Aadhaar itself, but whether a masked copy is enough is up to the organisation asking. Some services need your full number to verify it. If you are not sure, ask them before you send a copy.',
    ],
    [
      'Is my Aadhaar uploaded anywhere?',
      'No. The file is opened, read and masked in your browser, and never leaves your device. The text recognition that finds the number also runs on your device.',
    ],
    [
      'Can I mask a PAN card or other ID too?',
      'Yes. Drag over anything you want hidden on a PAN card, passport, voter ID, driving licence or bank statement. Only Aadhaar numbers are found automatically.',
    ],
    [
      'Why does my PDF come back as images?',
      'A black box drawn on top of a PDF leaves the text underneath, where anyone can copy it out. Turning each page into an image with the box burned in removes the hidden text for good.',
    ],
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Hide the first 8 digits of your Aadhaar number, or anything else, before you share a copy. It all happens on
    your device; nothing is uploaded.
  </Fragment>

  <form id="tool" class="tool" novalidate>
    <section class="panel glass">
      <h2><span>1</span> Pick your Aadhaar or other ID</h2>
      <label class="drop" id="drop">
        <input id="file" type="file" accept="image/*,.heic,.heif,.tif,.tiff,application/pdf,.pdf" />
        <strong>Choose a photo, scan or PDF</strong>
        <span>or drop it here. JPG, PNG, WebP, HEIC (iPhone), AVIF, TIFF, GIF, BMP or PDF.</span>
      </label>
      <p id="file-status" class="hint" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
      <p id="file-error" class="error" role="alert" hidden></p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel glass" id="edit" hidden>
      <h2><span>2</span> Check what's hidden</h2>
      <p id="detect" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <div class="stage" id="pages"></div>
      <div class="result">
        <p class="hint">Drag over anything else to hide it. Tap a box to remove it.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <button id="undo" class="btn" type="button" disabled>Undo</button>
          <button id="clear" class="btn" type="button" disabled>Clear</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">
        Older Aadhaar letters and cards have a QR code that holds the full number. If yours predates UIDAI's Secure
        QR code, or you aren't sure, drag a box over the QR code too.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel glass" id="finish" hidden>
      <h2><span>3</span> Add a note and download</h2>
      <label class="field">
        Add a note across the copy (optional)
        <input id="note" type="text" maxlength="80" placeholder="For KYC with ABC Bank only, 2 Nov 2026" />
      </label>
      <p class="hint">
        Write who the copy is for and today's date, so it can't easily be reused for anything else.
      </p>
      <p id="pdf-hint" class="hint" hidden>
        Each page comes back as a picture. A box drawn over a PDF in an editor leaves the text underneath it, where
        anyone can copy it out; turning the page into a picture removes it.
      </p>
      <div class="result">
        <p id="result" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <a id="download" class="btn primary" download hidden>Download</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </form>

  <Explainer title="What is masked Aadhaar?">
    <li>
      UIDAI, which issues Aadhaar, <a
        href="https://www.uidai.gov.in/283-faqs/aadhaar-online-services/e-aadhaar/1887-what-is-masked-aadhaar.html"
        >defines masked Aadhaar</a
      > as a copy where the first 8 digits of the number are replaced and only the last 4 stay visible. A hotel, a
      landlord or a bank can still tell which Aadhaar it is, but whoever gets hold of the copy doesn't have your full
      number. If you have an e-Aadhaar, you can also download a masked one from myAadhaar.
    </li>
    <li>
      Nothing is uploaded. Your file is opened, read and masked in your browser, and the text recognition that finds
      the number runs on your device too.
    </li>
    <li>
      A PDF comes back as pictures of its pages. Drawing a black box over a PDF in most editors only adds a shape on
      top: the number is still in the file as text, and copying it gets it back. Here every page becomes a picture
      with the box burned in, put back together at its original size, so there is no text left to copy.
    </li>
    <li>
      It works on any ID: PAN, passport, voter ID, driving licence or a bank statement. Automatic detection only looks
      for Aadhaar numbers, so on anything else, drag over what you want hidden.
    </li>
  </Explainer>
</Tool>

<script>
  import { findAadhaar, type Box } from '../../lib/aadhaar';
  import { openImage } from '../../lib/decode';
  import { isPdf, openPdf, PdfPasswordError, renderPage } from '../../lib/pdf';

  /** One page of the file; width and height are in PDF points, so the output keeps the original page size. */
  type Page = { source: HTMLCanvasElement; view: HTMLCanvasElement; width: number; height: number };
  type Mask = Box & { page: number };
  type Ctx = CanvasRenderingContext2D | OffscreenCanvasRenderingContext2D;

  const DPI = 200;
  const MAX_PAGES = 10;

  const $ = <T extends HTMLElement>(id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as T;
  const fileInput = $<HTMLInputElement>('file');
  const drop = $<HTMLLabelElement>('drop');
  const fileError = $<HTMLParagraphElement>('file-error');
  const fileStatus = $<HTMLParagraphElement>('file-status');
  const edit = $<HTMLElement>('edit');
  const finish = $<HTMLElement>('finish');
  const detect = $<HTMLParagraphElement>('detect');
  const stage = $<HTMLDivElement>('pages');
  const undo = $<HTMLButtonElement>('undo');
  const clear = $<HTMLButtonElement>('clear');
  const note = $<HTMLInputElement>('note');
  const pdfHint = $<HTMLParagraphElement>('pdf-hint');
  const result = $<HTMLParagraphElement>('result');
  const download = $<HTMLAnchorElement>('download');

  let file: { stem: string; pdf: boolean; pages: Page[] } | null = null;
  let masks: Mask[] = [];
  let history: Mask[][] = [];
  let url = '';
  let job = 0;

  function show(el: HTMLElement, text: string) {
    el.textContent = text;
    el.hidden = !text;
  }

  function paint(ctx: Ctx, i: number, draft?: Box) {
    const { source } = file!.pages[i]!;
    const { width: w, height: h } = source;
    ctx.drawImage(source, 0, 0);
    ctx.fillStyle = '#000';
    for (const m of masks) if (m.page === i) ctx.fillRect(m.x, m.y, m.w, m.h);
    const text = note.value.trim();
    if (text) {
      ctx.save();
      ctx.translate(w / 2, h / 2);
      ctx.rotate(-Math.atan2(h, w));
      const diagonal = Math.hypot(w, h);
      ctx.font = `600 100px system-ui, sans-serif`;
      // Long notes shrink to fit the diagonal; short ones stop at a size that still reads as a note.
      const size = Math.min(diagonal / 14, (100 * diagonal * 0.8) / ctx.measureText(text).width);
      ctx.font = `600 ${size}px system-ui, sans-serif`;
      ctx.textAlign = 'center';
      ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';
      ctx.fillStyle = 'rgb(185 28 28 / 0.45)';
      ctx.fillText(text, 0, 0);
      ctx.restore();
    }
    if (draft) {
      ctx.fillStyle = 'rgb(0 0 0 / 0.6)';
      ctx.fillRect(draft.x, draft.y, draft.w, draft.h);
    }
  }

  const redraw = (i: number, draft?: Box) => paint(file!.pages[i]!.view.getContext('2d')!, i, draft);

  const kb = (bytes: number) => (bytes < 1024 * 1024 ? `${Math.round(bytes / 1024)} KB` : `${(bytes / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(1)} MB`);

  async function render() {
    const mine = ++job;
    download.hidden = true;
    if (!file) return;
    const { pages, pdf, stem } = file;
    result.textContent = 'Making your copy…';
    // Painted afresh, so a box being dragged on the preview never ends up in the file.
    const jpegs: Blob[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < pages.length; i++) {
      const c = new OffscreenCanvas(pages[i]!.source.width, pages[i]!.source.height);
      paint(c.getContext('2d')!, i);
      jpegs.push(await c.convertToBlob({ type: 'image/jpeg', quality: 0.92 }));
      if (mine !== job) return;
    }
    let out = jpegs[0]!;
    if (pdf) {
      const { PDFDocument } = await import('pdf-lib');
      const doc = await PDFDocument.create();
      for (let i = 0; i < pages.length; i++) {
        const img = await doc.embedJpg(await jpegs[i]!.arrayBuffer());
        const { width, height } = pages[i]!;
        doc.addPage([width, height]).drawImage(img, { x: 0, y: 0, width, height });
      }
      out = new Blob([(await doc.save()) as BlobPart], { type: 'application/pdf' });
      if (mine !== job) return;
    }
    URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
    url = URL.createObjectURL(out);
    download.href = url;
    download.download = `${stem}-masked.${pdf ? 'pdf' : 'jpg'}`;
    download.textContent = `Download ${pdf ? 'PDF' : 'JPG'}`;
    download.hidden = false;
    const hidden = masks.length === 1 ? '1 area hidden' : `${masks.length} areas hidden`;
    const size = pdf ? `${pages.length} ${pages.length === 1 ? 'page' : 'pages'}` : `${pages[0]!.source.width} × ${pages[0]!.source.height} px`;
    result.textContent = `${size} · ${hidden} · ${kb(out.size)} · ${pdf ? 'PDF' : 'JPG'}`;
  }

  let timer = 0;
  const later = () => {
    download.hidden = true;
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = window.setTimeout(render, 250);
  };

  function commit(next: Mask[]) {
    history.push(masks);
    masks = next;
    undo.disabled = false;
    clear.disabled = !masks.length;
    file!.pages.forEach((_, i) => redraw(i));
    later();
  }

  async function findAll(mine: number) {
    const { pages } = file!;
    const found: Mask[] = [];
    try {
      for (let i = 0; i < pages.length; i++) {
        detect.textContent =
          pages.length > 1 ? `Looking for the Aadhaar number on page ${i + 1} of ${pages.length}…` : 'Looking for the Aadhaar number…';
        found.push(...(await findAadhaar(pages[i]!.source)).map((b) => ({ ...b, page: i })));
        if (mine !== opening) return;
      }
    } catch {
      if (mine === opening) detect.textContent = "Automatic detection didn't load. Drag over the number to hide it yourself.";
      return;
    }
    if (!found.length) {
      detect.textContent = "Couldn't find an Aadhaar number. Drag over it to hide it yourself.";
      return;
    }
    detect.textContent = `Found the Aadhaar number in ${found.length === 1 ? 'one place' : `${found.length} places`} and hid its first 8 digits. Check the preview below.`;
    commit([...masks, ...found]);
  }

  const canvasOf = (bitmap: ImageBitmap) => {
    const c = document.createElement('canvas');
    c.width = bitmap.width;
    c.height = bitmap.height;
    c.getContext('2d')!.drawImage(bitmap, 0, 0);
    bitmap.close();
    return c;
  };

  /** The pages, a message saying why the file can't be used, or null once a newer file has been picked. */
  async function readPages(picked: File, pdf: boolean, mine: number): Promise<Omit<Page, 'view'>[] | string | null> {
    if (!pdf) {
      const source = canvasOf(await openImage(picked));
      return [{ source, width: source.width, height: source.height }];
    }
    const doc = await openPdf(picked);
    try {
      if (doc.numPages > MAX_PAGES)
        return `"${picked.name}" has ${doc.numPages} pages; this tool takes up to ${MAX_PAGES}. Save just the pages with your ID as a new PDF, then pick that.`;
      const pages = [];
      for (let n = 1; n <= doc.numPages; n++) {
        show(fileStatus, `Opening page ${n} of ${doc.numPages}…`);
        const { canvas, width, height } = await renderPage(doc, n, DPI);
        if (mine !== opening) return null;
        pages.push({ source: canvas, width, height });
      }
      return pages;
    } finally {
      doc.loadingTask.destroy();
    }
  }

  let opening = 0;
  async function load(picked: File | undefined) {
    if (!picked) return;
    const mine = ++opening;
    show(fileError, '');
    show(fileStatus, `Opening "${picked.name}"…`);
    let pdf = false;
    let pages: Awaited<ReturnType<typeof readPages>>;
    try {
      pdf = await isPdf(picked);
      pages = await readPages(picked, pdf, mine);
    } catch (err) {
      pages =
        err instanceof PdfPasswordError
          ? `"${picked.name}" is locked with a password, as e-Aadhaar PDFs are. Open it in your PDF viewer, then print or save it as a PDF without the password, or take a screenshot, and pick that here.`
          : `Couldn't open "${picked.name}". Pick a photo, scan or PDF of your ID: JPG, PNG, WebP, HEIC, AVIF, TIFF, GIF, BMP or PDF.`;
    }
    // A slow PDF or HEIC must not land on top of a file picked after it.
    if (!pages || mine !== opening) return;
    show(fileStatus, '');
    if (typeof pages === 'string') return show(fileError, pages);
    stage.replaceChildren();
    file = {
      stem: picked.name.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '') || 'id',
      pdf,
      pages: pages.map((p, i) => {
        const view = document.createElement('canvas');
        view.width = p.source.width;
        view.height = p.source.height;
        view.style.setProperty('--ratio', String(view.width / view.height));
        view.tabIndex = 0;
        view.setAttribute('aria-label', `Page ${i + 1}. Drag to hide an area; tap a box to remove it.`);
        listen(view, i);
        stage.append(view);
        return { ...p, view };
      }),
    };
    masks = [];
    history = [];
    undo.disabled = clear.disabled = true;
    pdfHint.hidden = !pdf;
    edit.hidden = finish.hidden = false;
    file.pages.forEach((_, i) => redraw(i));
    later();
    findAll(mine);
  }

  const hit = (i: number, x: number, y: number) =>
    masks.findLastIndex((m) => m.page === i && x >= m.x && x <= m.x + m.w && y >= m.y && y <= m.y + m.h);

  function listen(view: HTMLCanvasElement, i: number) {
    const at = (e: PointerEvent) => {
      const r = view.getBoundingClientRect();
      return { x: ((e.clientX - r.left) * view.width) / r.width, y: ((e.clientY - r.top) * view.height) / r.height, cx: e.clientX, cy: e.clientY };
    };
    let from: ReturnType<typeof at> | null = null;
    let draft: Box | undefined;
    view.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {
      view.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
      from = at(e);
      draft = undefined;
    });
    view.addEventListener('pointermove', (e) => {
      const p = at(e);
      if (!from) {
        view.style.cursor = hit(i, p.x, p.y) >= 0 ? 'pointer' : '';
        return;
      }
      // A few pixels of wobble is still a tap.
      if (!draft && Math.hypot(p.cx - from.cx, p.cy - from.cy) < 6) return;
      draft = { x: Math.min(from.x, p.x), y: Math.min(from.y, p.y), w: Math.abs(p.x - from.x), h: Math.abs(p.y - from.y) };
      redraw(i, draft);
    });
    view.addEventListener('pointerup', (e) => {
      if (!from) return;
      const p = at(e);
      const k = hit(i, p.x, p.y);
      if (draft) commit([...masks, { ...draft, page: i }]);
      else if (k >= 0) commit(masks.filter((_, j) => j !== k));
      from = null;
      draft = undefined;
    });
    view.addEventListener('pointercancel', () => {
      from = null;
      draft = undefined;
      redraw(i);
    });
    view.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key !== 'z' || !(e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) || undo.disabled) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      undo.click();
    });
  }

  undo.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const prev = history.pop();
    if (!prev || !file) return;
    masks = prev;
    undo.disabled = !history.length;
    clear.disabled = !masks.length;
    file.pages.forEach((_, i) => redraw(i));
    later();
  });
  clear.addEventListener('click', () => file && masks.length && commit([]));
  note.addEventListener('input', () => {
    if (!file) return;
    file.pages.forEach((_, i) => redraw(i));
    later();
  });

  fileInput.addEventListener('change', () => load(fileInput.files?.[0]));
  drop.addEventListener('dragover', (e) => e.preventDefault());
  drop.addEventListener('drop', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    load(e.dataTransfer?.files[0]);
  });
  $<HTMLFormElement>('tool').addEventListener('submit', (e) => e.preventDefault());
  // On a slow connection a file can be picked before this script has loaded and started listening.
  load(fileInput.files?.[0]);
</script>

<style>
  /* Without these the full-resolution canvases size the grid tracks and burst the panel. */
  .stage {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .stage :global(canvas) {
    display: block;
    /* As wide as the panel, but a tall page stops at most of the screen's height. */
    width: min(100%, 80vh * var(--ratio));
    height: auto;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--border);
    cursor: crosshair;
    touch-action: none;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
